<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35354" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpessĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				bearing</i>, <i>suffering</i>, <i>enduring</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harum rerum perpessio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rab. Perd. 5, 16</span></i>
			: laborum, id. Inv.  2, 54, 163: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum arduarum ac difficilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 1, 15, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fortitudinis patientia et perpessio et
					tolerantia rami sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 67, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malae valetudinis et dolorum gravissimorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 66, 47</span></i>
			.</div>
